[Music]  [Music]  i'm a little late to the party on this  one but it has been a month since i  released a video so i'm a little out of  the routine but i wanted to make  something  finally after all this time the silence  from the developers of the division 2  has broken  on the 31st of march this tweet came out  today we have an important update from  the division 2 development team to share  with you it goes on to talk about season  9 the first season of year 4. and while  they aren't giving a date yet they  announced a pts for the update that  starts well now or a day or so ago to be  fair  if you weren't aware pts stands for  public test server the developers use  this as a way to test the updates before  anything goes live in the main game a  test version of the game  after receiving player feedback this  gives them the opportunity to tweak  adjust or fix anything that isn't  working as intended  given how long it's been i would say  that there will be a lot more people  jumping into this bts than normal  if you are wanting to give this a go you  can find the download in ubisoft connect  right below your games  unfortunately this is pc only due to the  limitations with xbox and sony and their  upload process  the pts is coming in three phases phase  one countdown and expertise phase two  new gear and balance adjustments phase  three  all of the above plus bug fixes  following phase one and two  currently we're in phase one playing  through the new game mode countdown and  trying out the new expertise leveling  system  i'm going to cover this a bit more in  another video where i'll give my  experience and thoughts that i should  have out in the next day or so  but i'll give you a little bit of a  rundown of what the game mode is all  about however some of the footage has  been played in the background right now  countdown is a new eight player pve in  game mode  two cells of four shd agents are  deployed at a power plant to prevent a  lockdown  there is a 15 minute timer that the  agents are working against where they  need to secure the site before it's too  late  when a couple of objectives have been  completed the agents can then extract  but this is where a familiar enemy makes  themselves known the hunters  while countdown is intended for eight  players and there is matchmaking you can  start with a smaller group and even run  it solo however there isn't any scaling  down for smaller teams you will still be  taking on the same difficulty and number  of enemies  i covered how expertise will work in a  previous video that i will link in the  description and it should be in the top  right of the screen right now  i'm pretty sure i get extra youtube  points for linking and referencing my  own videos so i'm just going to pat  myself in the back for that one  expertise is another progression system  outside of the shd levels and it also  provides a way to further customize your  builds for even greater build diversity  some may not think so but build  diversity is one of the key features of  the division that makes it unique i  would say that the bulk of you out there  who played this game for the most part  is because of the large number of  options you have when kitting out your  character otherwise you'd just be  playing any old third person shooter  like heartlands is unfortunately looking  like it could become even meta builds  can be counted you just need to think  outside of the box  basically anything that adds build  diversity is only a good thing for the  division  with the expertise system through  leveling the weapons and gear that you  use you can improve the performance of  select items  reading exactly what they stated this  feature is composed of two types of  progression systems the expertise level  and the proficiency rank  each eligible item has a proficiency  rank which can be increased either  through donations or kill xp  only when an item reaches the highest  proficiency rank possible will the agent  become proficient with it and be able to  increase the grade of the individual  items of that type  each type has the same amount of  proficiency ranks  additionally each agent has a unique  expertise level which increases as the  proficiency ranks are gained in more  item types  summing up weapons gear and skills now  have a new ranking system that we can  level up through using them in normal  gameplay  leveling up items will increase your  overall expertise level in turn granting  you something that you can use to  increase the base stats of an item of  your choosing  again check out my video i feel like i  explained it far more clearly  this update will also be coming with a  bunch of new gear and weapons  now i don't want to just sit here and  read from a page that i could just  direct you towards i don't think that's  why you're here but i will point out one  of the ones that intrigues me  catharsis exotic mask  talent vicious cycle  taking damage stacks to a cap of thirty  each stack gains one percent weapon  damage  taking damage at max stacks triggers a  purge removing all stacks and status  effects and then dropping a healing  cloud which restores five percent of max  armor for ten seconds to all allies in  the cloud  i can see this being potentially quite  useful especially with a new countdown  game mode  i'll post a link to all of the new gear  and weapons in the description however  if for some reason you did want to read  through them on a youtube video i'll  display them on screen now accompanied  by the sound of a young child playing a  recorder  [Music]  [Music]  be  as expected this update will also  feature a number of balancing and  gameplay adjustments  like the new gear and weapons you can  find a list of these using the same link  in the description but i would like to  point out that there has been a  considerable amount of focus on shields  the developers have recognized how  unbalanced they've been for quite some  time now and that they have been  considered a requirement in both pve and  pvp so the way some talents now interact  with shields like nsync and intimidate  have been considerably reduced or  removed a good move in my opinion  [Music]  it has been a long time since we've seen  any updates to the division so  regardless of what you think of what  i've just briefly run through this is a  good thing to see some love being put  into the game i will however say that  none of this is what makes me so excited  for the next 12 months it's not that i  haven't enjoyed what i've seen so far  but that there is more to the story  when i first heard that there is a new  game mode being created and some  adjustments and balancing going on it  didn't really fulfill me with hope that  the franchise i love had any future just  that it was getting a small update  however after yannick the creative  director of the division 2 posted this  up on twitter  yes i am just going to read this out  because i think it's important to hear  agents before we all jump on the pts  there's something i'd like you to keep  in mind  the year we've spent working on the game  in silence was not spent making one  gigantic comeback update it was spent  organizing and preparing for continuous  support of the game the importance of  this update is not in its size but in  heralding a return to normal with more  to come after that  if this update doesn't contain the  changes or content you're hoping for  just remember that there are more  updates coming throughout the year for  now i hope we can all share a happy  moment and rejoice that support for the  game is resuming we're live again  so this is potentially just the first of  many updates we'll be seeing as we know  support for the game was supposed to end  quite some time ago with no knowledge on  whether we'd be seeing any sort of  addition to the franchise  while i'm happy with what i'm seeing so  far from the pts continued support for  the foreseeable future is far greater  news to me  anyway i'm going to wrap this one up  apologies there's been such a drought  and uploads for me in the last month or  so real life has been throwing some very  interesting things my way as of recently  and i've struggled to find the time  but i plan on putting some extra effort  going forward i've really been missing  the creative outlet  so once again thank you very much for  watching if you made it this far and  i'll catch in the next one cheers  [Music]  oh

